              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to meet, then the Persian for to hurry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پله برقی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پله برقی (pelle-barqi) — \"an escalator\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در ایستگاه مترو پله برقی خراب بود. Dar istgâh-e metro pelle-barqi kharâb bud. The escalator at the metro station was out of order."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally 'electric stairs': pelle 'step' + barqi 'electric'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pelle-barqi is built from pelle 'step, stair', whose origin is not settled, and barqi 'electric', from barq 'electricity', borrowed from Arabic barq 'lightning, flashing' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
