              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسیر (masir) — \"a route, a way\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسیر (masir) این اتوبوس خیلی طولانی است. Masir-e in otobus kheyli tulâni ast. This bus's route is very long."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dar masir — on the way, en route."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "masir was borrowed from Arabic and is usually traced to Arabic masīr 'going, the way of a journey'. EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
        },
