          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جا ماندن (jâ mândan) — \"to miss (a bus, a train); to be left behind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دیر رسیدم و از اتوبوس جا ماندم. Dir residam va az otobus jâ mândam. I arrived late and missed the bus."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jâ 'place' + mândan 'to stay'. Things can be left behind too: kifam dar tâksi jâ mând."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jâ mândan is built from jâ 'place', inherited from Middle Persian gyāg (EtymDB), and mândan 'to remain', which EtymDB traces to Middle Persian: to stay behind in one's place."
            }
          ]
        },
